{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0901"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/pop-rock","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/zz-r2-music-stage__pop-rock.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",880],["+","**Christine McVie** (1943–2022) wrote her anthems inside a band. After singing and playing piano with the blues group Chicken Shack, she officially joined Fleetwood Mac in 1970 as the band's first female singer, years before Stevie Nicks arrived. For the group she wrote \"Say You Love Me\", \"Don't Stop\", \"Everywhere\" and \"Little Lies\", as well as \"Songbird\", the quiet piano ballad that closes the first side of Rumours (1977) and that she wrote alone in half an hour one night.\n\n"],["=",109],["+","\n| “Songbird” | Christine McVie (Fleetwood Mac) | 1977 |"],["=",62]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",898],["+","**Christine McVie** (1943–2022) schrieb ihre Hymnen innerhalb einer Band. Nachdem sie bei der Bluesgruppe Chicken Shack gesungen und Klavier gespielt hatte, wurde sie 1970 offiziell Mitglied von Fleetwood Mac und damit die erste Sängerin der Band, Jahre bevor Stevie Nicks dazukam. Für die Gruppe schrieb sie „Say You Love Me“, „Don't Stop“, „Everywhere“ und „Little Lies“ sowie „Songbird“, die leise Klavierballade am Ende der ersten Seite von Rumours (1977), die sie eines Nachts allein in einer halben Stunde schrieb.\n\n"],["=",109],["+","\n| „Songbird“ | Christine McVie (Fleetwood Mac) | 1977 |"],["=",62]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0901"},"reason":"a0901 (body): \"Tracy Chapman was busking in Harvard Square when she was discovered\" → she was a Tufts student who busked in Harvard Square and was discovered by fellow student Brian Koppelman in 1987 — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tracy_Chapman_(album)","by":"enrich batch 130","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a0469-a0913.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tracy_Chapman_(album"}]},
